      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Lorenzo purchased a box of cereal and some strawberries at the grocery store.\nLorenzo paid \\$2 for the box of cereal and \\$1.90 per pound for the strawberries. If Lorenzo paid a\ntotal of \\$9.60 for the box of cereal and the strawberries, which of the following equations can be\nused to find $p$, the number of pounds of strawberries Lorenzo purchased？ (Assume there is no\nsales tax.)"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-2f88ecf50fcb4001b4736803ad6ac70e",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m1-q1"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.90 p+2=9.60$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.90 p - 2=9.60$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.90+2 p=9.60$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.90 - 2 p=9.60$$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
